  "worked_solution": "For our Fourier cosine series, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=5{x}^{2}+2$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(5{x}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{[\\frac{5{x}^{3}}{3}+2x]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(\\frac{5{\\pi }^{3}}{3}+2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =2(\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{3}+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
